<title>USA: Issing urges Bonn to convert debt to Euros in 1999.</title>
<headline>Issing urges Bonn to convert debt to Euros in 1999.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank Chief Economist Otmar Issing said Monday that Germany should make every effort to convert the bulk of its outstanding debt to be denominated in the single European currency from its launch year in 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;I think we should find a way so that the important part of public debt can be translated into Euros,&quot; Issing told a conference in Washington.</p>
<p>France has already pledged to convert its debt from 1999 but Germany has delayed a decision due to the fractured nature of its banking market.</p>
<p>An early conversion by Germany is seen as important for the liquidity of debt markets in the new Euro as soon as it is created.</p>
</text>
